  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A Severe Thunderstorm Watch is now in effect \nfor Delmarva, southern New Jersey, and Chester county.\n\nSevere thunderstorms over western and central Pennsylvania are \ntracking to the east-southeast, and will move into an unstable \nairmass with DCAPE from 1000-1400 J/kg over southeast \nPennsylvania, southern New Jersey and Delmarva. SBCAPE Values \nare in excess of 2000J/kg, and there is 30-40 kt of 0-6 km Bulk \nShear. Thunderstorms should hold together enough despite lack of\ndiurnal heating due to the instability over the area to produce\nsevere weather, generally in the form of damaging winds, but \ncannot rule out large hail. \n\nIn addition, local flash flooding is possible with the \nthunderstorms. There is limited confidence in which areas will \nreceive any flooding, and also with greater storm motion, it's \nprobable that flooding may be limited. For these reasons, we \nhave not considered any flood watches attm. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...The Labor Day Weekend will feature mostly dry \nweather with at or below normal temperatures and lower humidity.\n\nBy Saturday, the trend among model guidance shows the frontal \nboundary south of our region, with Canadian high pressure \nbuilding in across the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic. This will \nlargely end any shower and thunderstorm potential. Thus, Labor \nDay Weekend is still shaping up to feature nice weather, with \ntemperatures trending at or slightly below normal and lower \nhumidity.",
